<title>SWEDEN: Atlas Copco says to buy Thome-Crepelle.</title>
<headline>Atlas Copco says to buy Thome-Crepelle.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish engineer Atlas Copco AB said on Wednesday its unit Atlas Copco France Holding SA agreed to acquire French compressor company Thome-Crepelle from Compagnie Fives-Lille.  </p>
<p>The agreement was preliminary, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition is subject to necessary approvals and to the reaching of a mutually acceptable purchase agreement,&quot; Atlas Copco said.</p>
<p>Thome-Crepelle, of Lille, has 200 employees. Last year's turnover was 196 million francs.</p>
<p>&quot;It is planned that Atlas Copco will take over Thome-Crepelle before the end of the second quarter of 1997,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
